# 7. A spec's text, legible.

# Given: a spec with a code block and a table inside a list item, and a sentence with inline code.
exec kiln queue x
exec kiln run
stdout '^x: landed on main'

# When: the developer opens its spec text.
term 120 40 kiln tui x
screen 'builds of x · approved once'
keys s
screen '^x · as approved at [0-9a-f]{12}$'

# Then: a blank line separates the code block and the table from the text after each, as in the spec's source,
screen '^  ```go\n  func X\(\) int \{ return 42 \}\n  ```\n\n  The text after the code block\.$'
screen '^  \| X +\| 42 +\|\n\n  The text after the table\.$'

# and inline code has no background color.
screen '^The view shows `kiln tui` and `kiln run` as written\.$'
color background none '`kiln tui`'
color background none '`kiln run`'

-- go.mod --
module example.com/scratch

go 1.27
-- .kiln/kiln.json --
{"gate": ["go vet ./...", "go test ./..."], "rounds": 0}
-- .kiln/specs/x.md --
# Spec 1: x

Status: Approved, 2026-11-09

## Overview

The view shows `kiln tui` and `kiln run` as written.

- **A code block.** Inside this item:

  ```go
  func X() int { return 42 }
  ```

  The text after the code block.

- **A table.** Inside this item:

  | name | answer |
  |------|--------|
  | X    | 42     |

  The text after the table.

